<header><p class="st-kicker">nomadic confederation · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Aorsi</h1><p class="st-meta">200 BCE – 100 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A powerful Sarmatian people between the Don and the Caspian, whose control of caravan routes made them rich in gold and allies of Rome.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Aorsi emerge in Greek sources in the 2nd century BCE as one of the leading Sarmatian groups, descended from the earlier steppe populations of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sarmatians">Sauromatae</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> divides them into a western group on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/don-river">Don</a> and the 'Upper Aorsi' further east, who ruled most of the Caspian shore.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> reports that the Aorsi could field 200,000 horsemen and that the Upper Aorsi wore gold because they carried Indian and Babylonian goods on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camels</a> from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenia">Armenia</a> and Media. They were pastoral nomads organised under kings, and they appear in the politics of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bosporan-kingdom">Bosporan Kingdom</a>, fighting with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siraces">Siraces</a> in 49 CE under their king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunones">Eunones</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>From the late 1st century CE the Aorsi fade from the record as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/alans">Alans</a> rose to dominate the same steppes. Most historians think they were absorbed into the Alan confederation, which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> overran in the 370s.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/aorsi.jpg" alt="Aorsi" width="320" height="188"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Lessman (Contact!) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East-Hem_100bc.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>200 BCE – 100 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>nomadic confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Eunones, Spadines</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Iranian steppe religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sarmatian (Eastern Iranian)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a>, <a href="/countries/kazakhstan">Kazakhstan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Aorsoi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-50&amp;focus=aorsi" aria-label="Aorsi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5632 204 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Aorsi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5952 460h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5952 460h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Russia. <a href="/atlas?year=-50&amp;focus=aorsi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
